  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gweru Urban Resilience Building (GURB)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to strengthen the resilience of communities, women and youth through the development of safe markets, economic empowerment of youths and promotion of an enabling policy environment. The project uses an integrated approach that combines the following: (a) technical skills training; (b) market upgrading; (c) training for transformation (T4T); (d) business and entrepreneurial skills development; (e) policy advocacy. The project is of significantly aligns with key sustainable development goals (SDGs); SDG 2: Zero Hunger; SDG 4: Quality Education; SDG 8: Decent work and economic growth; SDG 9: Industry, Innovation, and Infrastructure; SDG 13: climate action and action; and SDG 17: partnerships.  It also aligns with the government&#x2019;s National Development Strategy (NDS 1) and is in sync with Gweru municipality&#x2019;s development plans. Silveira House will partner with Gweru City Council to upgrade stalled works on the Mutapa market, making it safer and conducive for women and other vulnerable groups, establish a youth hub in one of the city&#x2019;s high density surburbs where trainings will take place and equipment will be stored for continued use by youths beyond project life span. It will also partner with CCJP Gweru and CARITAS Gweru combining efforts on youth mobilisation, policy advocacy, safe markets education and awareness and continuous monitoring of training and infrastructure works.</narrative>
  </description>
